      "id": "bk2-der-107",
      "q": "Fever, facial swelling, eosinophilia and hepatitis 4 weeks after starting a drug with HHV-6 reactivation is?",
      "o": [
        "DRESS syndrome",
        "Anaphylaxis",
        "Serum sickness",
        "Acute viral hepatitis"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "exp": "DRESS has 2 to 6 week latency with eosinophilia, atypical lymphocytes, organ injury and viral reactivation.",
      "r": [
        "Correct. Late rash with eosinophils and hepatitis.",
        "Incorrect. That is immediate with airway collapse.",
        "Incorrect. That gives arthralgia with complexes.",
        "Incorrect. That lacks rash-eosinophil timing."
      ],
      "kp": "Late rash with eosinophils and hepatitis is DRESS.",
      "topic": "der-drug-reactions"
