      "id": "bk2-der-108",
      "q": "Sudden fever with dozens of non-follicular sterile pustules on red swollen skin days after a drug is?",
      "o": [
        "Generalised pustular psoriasis",
        "Bacterial folliculitis",
        "Subcorneal pustular dermatosis",
        "Acute generalised exanthematous pustulosis"
      ],
      "a": 3,
      "exp": "AGEP erupts within days of drugs with neutrophilia and rapid peeling resolution after withdrawal.",
      "r": [
        "Incorrect. That follows withdrawal in psoriatics.",
        "Incorrect. That centres on follicles with bacteria.",
        "Incorrect. That is chronic annular.",
        "Correct. Drug-timed sterile pustules."
      ],
      "kp": "Drug-timed pustules with fever mean AGEP.",
      "topic": "der-drug-reactions"
